  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Bilateral Nostro & Vostro Settlement Principle",
      "items": [
        "Nostro Account (Our money at Partner Bank): AuraBank defines a pre-funded GL account (e.g. ACC-NOSTRO-BANK-B) in its T24 Master DB. When Alice sends money to Bank B, AuraBank debits Alice and credits its Nostro clearing buffer.",
        "Vostro Account (Partner Bank money with AuraBank): Partner Bank maintains a corresponding Vostro account (ACC-VOSTRO-AURABANK). Partner Bank debits the Vostro buffer and credits Bob's personal account.",
        "Zero Third-Party Dependency: No centralized clearing switch needed. Both capstone groups simply agree on a pre-seeded balance (e.g. 10,000,000 PHP) and an authenticated JSON wire contract."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Outbound & Inbound Inter-Bank Transaction Lifecycle",
      "items": [
        "Leg 1 (Domestic Debit): AuraBank Transfer Orchestrator invokes internal T24 CBS POST /api/v1/cbs/funds-transfer (Debit: Alice, Credit: ACC-NOSTRO-BANK-B).",
        "Leg 2 (Inter-Bank Wire Dispatch): Orchestrator sends authenticated HTTP REST payload with API Key header and idempotency token to Partner Bank POST /api/v1/transfers/interbank/inward.",
        "Leg 3 (Beneficiary Credit): Partner Bank CBS executes internal funds transfer (Debit: ACC-VOSTRO-AURABANK, Credit: Bob) and returns 200 OK with partner transaction reference.",
        "Saga Compensation (Rollback on Failure): If Partner Bank returns 404/500 or times out, AuraBank Orchestrator calls T24 POST /api/v1/cbs/reversal to immediately restore Alice's funds."
      ]
    }
  ]
